       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you're taking responsibility for it. But 50 mg of amlodipine is a dose I'd expect to cause serious harm, and I don't have a clinical rationale that would justify it. I'd rather not put it into the system on my own.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 10 mg by mouth once daily (the maximum) right now. You or the team can titrate later if needed.\n- **Use a different order route.** If you're sure about 50 mg, you could enter it directly in the order-entry system. It would then go through pharmacist verification and the hospital's high-dose override process, which is the right check for an order like this.\n- **Add a rationale.** If something specific justifies this dose, such as a protocol or a toxicology consult, tell me what it is. I'll reconsider and include it in the order note.\n\nIf the target is stronger blood pressure control, I can also help enter an add-on agent from another class instead of a higher amlodipine dose."
      }
